Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:02:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bot): share one quota balance with the website

Adds /buy and /usage, and meters chat messages against the same balance
konkred.xyz uses, so a user's credit is identical on both surfaces.

- bot/quota_client.py: client for the website's /api/internal/quota/* contract.
  Uses httpx (already a dependency) rather than adding aiohttp. Identity is
  always telegram:<id> derived from the update, never from user text.
- bot/quota_handlers.py: /usage shows the shared balance; /buy links to the
  checkout page with the TRC20 wrong-network warning. Payment stays on the
  website so the invoice and warning are read on a real page.
- bot/main.py: quota_router is registered BEFORE the chat router, otherwise
  the catch-all text handler would swallow /buy and /usage.
- bot/handlers.py: reserves one message BEFORE calling the gateway, so an
  exhausted user never consumes provider credit; refunds on GatewayError, on
  an unexpected exception, and on a 200 with empty content.
- render.yaml: KONKRED_SITE_URL and INTERNAL_API_KEY for the bot service.

Design note: an HTTP contract is used instead of giving this bot PostgreSQL
credentials. Direct access would duplicate the spend/trial/refund rules in a
second language, and the first divergence between the two is a billing bug.

Fails open by design: if the quota service is unreachable the bot still
answers. Losing revenue on a few messages beats an outage.

Tests: 97 pass (88 existing + 9 new). scripts/check_python_imports.py OK.
